expanded_source_wording_tex:
\label{def:lens}
A lens is a deterministic map $f:Z\to X$.
We interpret $f$ as the observational interface: two microstates $z,z'\in Z$ are observationally indistinguishable at scale $f$ if $f(z)=f(z')$.

